::node[crm_agent]
->[:role=skill]
->[:traverse=priority:high]
->[:requires=crm_agent_capture]
->[:requires=crm_agent_resume_pack]
->[:keywords=crm, contacts, relationship, catch me up, who is, track contact, contact management]

::traverse
  priority    = high
  entry       = crm_agent
  depth-limit = 3

::dense
Contact tracker: person nodes, interaction log, "catch me up on X" resume packs.

::steps
1. On "catch me up on <person>", run crm_agent_resume_pack to build a context pack from memory.
2. After any meeting or email exchange, run crm_agent_capture to log the interaction.
3. Use crm_agent_enrich to pull additional context from Gmail history.

::node[crm_agent_capture]
->[:role=skill]
->[:keywords=capture interaction, log meeting, remember conversation, interaction log, record meeting]

::dense
Log an interaction with a contact as a person memory node with an episode edge.

::full
Use memory_write_node to write an episode node:
- role: event
- edges: ["->[:involves=<person-slug>]", "->[:about=<topic-slug>]"]
- dense: One-sentence summary of the interaction (date, key outcome).
Also update the person node: role=person, dense updated with latest known role/context.

::node[crm_agent_resume_pack]
->[:role=skill]
->[:keywords=catch me up on, who is X, context pack, person history, relationship context, last contact]

::dense
Build a memory resume pack for a named person: recent interactions, role, topics discussed.

::full
Steps:
1. Search memory for person slug via memory_search "<person-name>".
2. Walk Stage-C graph from the person node (involves edges → related topics, decisions).
3. Return a resume pack: person summary, last 3 interactions, open topics.

::node[crm_agent_enrich]
->[:role=skill]
->[:keywords=enrich contact, find email history, people node, involves edge, gmail history]

::dense
Enrich a contact's person node with Gmail interaction history (last 5 threads).

::full
1. Search Gmail for threads from/to <email> (last 30 days).
2. For each thread, extract subject + outcome (1 sentence).
3. Append each as an interaction episode node linked to the person node.
